    "body": "The account director approves a account plan review date exception, while the preparer records the evidence and the time of the handoff. No deadline widens the account plan review date authority beyond the scope written in the case template. The account plan review date delegation note names the deputy, the period, and the record that ends the delegation. The account plan review date reviewer can see who approved, what they approved, and when the approval expires. Review pass 3.1: the account team files the account plan review date evidence.\n\nThe account plan review date authority note names the account director as approver and records any delegation with its end date. A account plan review date role change triggers a review of queue access before the next case is assigned. A standing instruction for account plan review date needs an end date, and the account director confirms it is still current. The account director owns the account plan review date decision; the assistant may prepare, compare, and route but not approve. Review pass 3.2: the account team files the account plan review date evidence."
